    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Misuzu no Kuni</strong> is a linear visual novel with no branching choices.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The story is presented through visuals and sound, and progresses by clicking through the scenes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Estimated playtime is around 2 to 3 hours.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A replay gallery feature is included, allowing players to revisit visuals and listen to the original soundtrack experienced in the game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The story is set in an alternate version of late 20th century Japan, where an imaginary autonomous region called the \u201cLand of the Tengu\u201d exists.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There, a girl named Misuzu enters the country and joins the training of the Tengu, leading to a fantasy school drama.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Various fantasy elements appear throughout the story, including divine beast-like spirits called \u201cBake,\u201d a Tengu princess, and magical powers known as \u201cJintsuuriki.\u201d</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game is available in Japanese only.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Misuzu no Kuni</strong> is a linear visual novel with no branching choices.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The story is presented through visuals and sound, and progresses by clicking through the scenes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Estimated playtime is around 2 to 3 hours.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A replay gallery feature is included, allowing players to revisit visuals and listen to the original soundtrack experienced in the game.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The story is set in an alternate version of late 20th century Japan, where an imaginary autonomous region called the \u201cLand of the Tengu\u201d exists.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There, a girl named Misuzu enters the country and joins the training of the Tengu, leading to a fantasy school drama.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Various fantasy elements appear throughout the story, including divine beast-like spirits called \u201cBake,\u201d a Tengu princess, and magical powers known as \u201cJintsuuriki.\u201d</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game is available in Japanese only.</p>",
    "short_description": "Misuzu no Kuni is a kinetic visual novel with no choices or branching paths.Set in a late 20th-century Japan, it tells a traditional-style fantasy school drama.In this world, a special autonomous territory known as the Land of the Tengu exists within Japan.Supported language: Japanese only.",
